NAME
       reboot - restart the machine; poweroff - switch it off

SYNOPSIS
       reboot [-f]
       poweroff [-f]

DESCRIPTION
       reboot stops every service in order, unmounts the file systems and
       starts the machine again. poweroff does the same and then switches
       the machine off. On RHEL 9 both are short forms of systemctl reboot
       and systemctl poweroff. Only root can run them.

       Before a reboot on the exam, make sure your changes will survive it:
       services enabled, file systems in /etc/fstab (check with mount -a),
       network settings saved in the connection profile, booleans set with
       -P, firewall rules made --permanent.

       In the rd.break emergency shell systemd is not running yet. There,
       leave with exit (twice) to let the boot continue, or force a restart
       with reboot -f.

OPTIONS
       -f, --force
              Restart or power off at once, without stopping the services.
              Only for emergencies: unsaved data is lost.

EXAMPLES
           reboot
           systemctl reboot
           poweroff

SEE ALSO
       shutdown(8), halt(8), systemctl(1)
